{"id":179162323572496,"type":"album","name":"Dots and Loops","artist":"Stereolab","year":1997,"weight":47,"info":{"cover":"https://cdn2.albumoftheyear.org/600x0/album/9447-dots-and-loops_020629.jpg","aoty":83,"aoty_user":86,"sputnik":4.15,"yt":"vbeJ4-OMorU","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/stereolab/dots-and-loops","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/9447-stereolab-dots-and-loops.php","sputnikmusic":"https://www.sputnikmusic.com/album/20065/Stereolab-Dots-and-Loops/"},"desc":"Dots and Loops is the fifth studio album by English-French rock band Stereolab. It was released on 22 September 1997 and was issued by Duophonic Records and Elektra Records. The band co-produced the album with John McEntire and Andi Toma, and recording took place in Chicago and Düsseldorf. The album explores jazz and electronic sounds, and is influenced by bossa nova and 1960s pop music. Its lyrics address matters such as consumerism, the \"spectacle\", materialism, and human interaction. Dots and Loops reached number 19 on the UK Albums Chart, as well as number 111 on the Billboard 200 chart in ."},"artist_ref":{"id":202804497084959,"name":"Stereolab","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Stereolab_%281994%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":207755761847598,"type":"genre","name":"Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":540,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":245950225873330,"type":"genre","name":"Post-Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":526,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":181296768148316,"type":"genre","name":"Digital Hardcore","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":404,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":99248936442916,"type":"genre","name":"Hard Dance","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":399,"yt":null,"src":"rym"},{"id":191043281221162,"type":"genre","name":"Brutal Prog","artist":null,"year":n